From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Duke Eagleman <301139544+jerricky26@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:46:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8010-j171: Enable the speakers

Describe the J171 speaker link as on J71b: MCA2 as clock provider in
the iOS TDM mode ("dsp_a", eight 16-bit slots), aud2 routed to pin2,
and the MAX98357A amplifiers modelled as one codec through their shared
SD_MODE line on AP GPIO 20.

The J171 ADT (iPadOS 18.7.11) matches J71b for everything this uses:
MCA2 at 0x20a0a8000 (size 0x4000) with its MCLK word at 0x20a002008,
IRQ 229, mca-version 5, clock gate ps_mca2, the aud2 to pin2 route,
SmartIO TX endpoint 0x2c (transfer 0x21, FIFO 0x180, trigger 0xcc), NCO
channel 2, and audio-control,max98357 with 4 channels enabled by AP
GPIO 20. /arm-io/mca2/audio-speaker has the same reg on both boards:
<0x1301 0x10008 0x0 0x10080 0x0 0xf 0x0 0x10100004 0x0>.

The NCO reference rate is not in the IPSW ADT (iBoot fills it in), so
this takes J71b's 800 MHz.

Tested on one J171: speaker-test on hw:0,0 at 48 kHz, S16_LE, 4
channels gives a clean tone on every slot with no kernel messages.
Slots 1 and 2 drive the bottom-left speaker, slots 3 and 4 the
bottom-right one. The earlier plain I2S description (format "i2s", no
maxim,tdm) gave loud static.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Duke Eagleman <301139544+jerricky26@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-j171.dts | 48 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-j171.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-j171.dts
index 6751bf3a4afd..0980fd0c0761 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-j171.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-j171.dts
@@ -11,4 +11,52 @@
 / {
 	compatible = "apple,j171", "apple,t8010", "apple,arm-platform";
 	model = "Apple iPad 7 (Wi-Fi)";
+
+	/* One logical codec models the amplifier bank's shared SD_MODE line. */
+	speaker_amps: amplifier {
+		compatible = "maxim,max98357a";
+		#sound-dai-cells = <0>;
+		maxim,tdm;
+		sdmode-gpios = <&pinctrl_ap 20 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+	};
+
+	sound {
+		compatible = "simple-audio-card";
+		simple-audio-card,name = "J171 Speakers";
+		simple-audio-card,format = "dsp_a";
+		simple-audio-card,bitclock-master = <&speaker_cpu>;
+		simple-audio-card,frame-master = <&speaker_cpu>;
+		simple-audio-card,widgets = "Speaker", "Speakers";
+		simple-audio-card,routing = "Speakers", "Speaker";
+		simple-audio-card,pin-switches = "Speakers";
+
+		speaker_cpu: simple-audio-card,cpu {
+			sound-dai = <&mca2>;
+		};
+
+		simple-audio-card,codec {
+			sound-dai = <&speaker_amps>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&mca2 {
+	apple,i2s-switch = <&i2s_switch 2 2>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&i2s_switch {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+/*
+ * The J171 ADT from the IPSW leaves the NCO reference rate for iBoot to fill
+ * in; this is the J71b rate, which J171 is assumed to share.
+ */
+&nco_clkref {
+	clock-frequency = <800000000>;
+};
+
+&nco {
+	status = "okay";
 };
